SUMMARY:The History and Geology of the Scarborough Bluffs!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nWelcome to Tor
 onto History Walks! This walking tour blends the human history and the nat
 ural history of the area. A fascinating tour\, so don't miss it. If you ar
 e new to Toronto then this tour is for you!\n\nThe Scarborough Bluffs is T
 oronto's best kept secret. Known as "Les Grands Ecores." by the French\, a
 nd in 1788 Alexander Aitken\, called the bluffs the High Lands. A hidden g
 em in Toronto which hides many secrets.\n\nElizabeth Simcoe named the Bluf
 fs the Scarborough Highlands in 1793 and had reminded Elizabeth Simcoe of 
 the limestone cliffs back in England\, in her own words from her diary:\n\
 n"The shore is extremely bold and has the appearance of chalk cliffs\, but
  I believe they are only white sand. They appeared so well that we talked 
 of building a summer residence there and calling it Scarborough."\n\nThe S
 carborough Bluffs extended west along the coastline of Lake Ontario toward
 s the town of York and later Toronto\, but vast areas along the western ed
 ge were razed for industrial and residential development. The formation of
  the chalk cliffs continues to shrink due to erosion.\n\nThe price of this
  tour is $15.00 per person\n\nThis extensive walking tour begins at Bluffe
 rs Park Road and Brimley Road South\, south of Kingston Road near the lake
  at the marina stop!\n\nThe 201 Bluffers Park Bus leaves Kennedy Subway St
 ation every 15 minutes.\n\nHope to see you there!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note:
  Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour
 ! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@g
 mail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/313008
 010/
