BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314148041@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260603T050342Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T111000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T141000
SUMMARY:Spring on the Historic Toronto Islands! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nFor summertime 
 fun\, it's hard to imagine a better place than the Toronto Islands. It's s
 o much more than a small amusement park\, Chelsea Beach\, and walking and 
 bike trails. It's about growing up in Toronto. About the ten minute ride o
 ver on the ferry boat\, and the memories that have made Toronto a summerti
 me city. It's a stretch of land that is historic and fascinating\, both ge
 ologically and socially as well. And a history that brings together the st
 ories of Toronto from its founding.\n\nThe Gibraltar Point Lighthouse was 
 constructed in 1809\, and is one of the oldest structures in Toronto. It i
 s best known for the ghost story of its murdered first keeper\, John Paul 
 Rademüller. But that's another story for another day.\n\nThe peninsula wa
 s partially severed by a storm in 1852\, which created a sandbar that was 
 dangerously thin\, and the peninsula became an island permanently by a vio
 lent storm that cut out the eastern channel\, two hotels on the island wer
 e also destroyed. The modern history of the Islands' begins here!\n\nThe I
 slands' have three main parts\, and all three have their historic elements
 \, the most being the western most island named for the Hanlan family. A s
 pectacular hotel\, "The Ned Hanlan" was built and a regatta course dredged
  out of the western lagoon. An amusement park followed\, and an airport af
 ter that!\n\nIt was also a residential enclave with most of the homes appe
 aring on Ward's and Centre Islands. By the 1950s these residential areas s
 tarted to disappear\, as the idea of increasing city parkland took shape.\
 n\n**Take a quick peek at my introduction video which follows at** https:/
 /youtu.be/hkVHx5Ol9qI\n\nThe tour begins and ends at the Jack Layton Ferry
  Terminal at the foot of Bay Street. We will meet inside the gates! And we
  will head over as a group\, so tickets must be bought before! Please meet
  10 minutes before the meetup time!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15
 .00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket pric
 e when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the followi
 ng email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314148
 041/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260406T144004Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T144004Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314146904@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260603T050342Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
SUMMARY:An Epic Journey: Dante's Inferno (LECTURE ON THE GO)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\nWe have an amazing "Lecture on the Go" series for 2026. New
  topics and fascinating stories abound! Join us and learn about the world 
 and keep active and warm and cool during the winter and summer months!\n\n
 I started this walking classroom when we were under that horrible cloud ca
 lled Covid. This series was popular and helped people get back into societ
 y and life.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series is open to members who have 
 purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's free for those members. If you
  wish to attend a lecture and you are not a yearly pass member then the pr
 ice **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nThis fourth lecture is focussed on the w
 ritings by the Italian poet Dante Alighieri. We are taken on an unexpected
  descent into a place where every choice\, mistake\, and hidden truth seem
 s to have a consequence. Dante finds himself lost\, but what follows is an
 ything but ordinary. He enters a world that is imaginative\, and strangely
  familiar.\n\nDante encounters a series of surprising scenes. The landscap
 e shifts\, the atmosphere deepens\, and the people he meets add a layer of
  realism that makes the experience personal. The structure of the story bu
 ilds in intensity\, revealing how each step downward uncovers something ne
 w.\n\nWhat makes this work so fascinating is not just its imagery\, but th
 e questions it raises. *Inferno* invites you to think differently about co
 nsequences\, and accountability\, and the way stories shape our understand
 ing. You may find yourself reconsidering ideas in new light.\n\nIn this le
 cture on the Go\, we’ll explore *Dante’s Inferno* in a way that reveal
 s its surprises. You’ll come away with a clear understanding of the jour
 ney\, and its themes\, and the remarkable way in which it was written. If 
 you’re curious about a story that continues to challenge this is one jou
 rney you won’t want to miss.\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\
 \*Philosophy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (June 
 2026)\n\\*Philosophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to D
 alai Lama - (July 2026)\nThe 1977 Disaster at Tenerife - (August 2026)\nLe
 gacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (
 September 2026)\n\nThis is the fourth event in the series! So book your pl
 ans now!\n\nThis event is for all levels and walkers\, there are a few ste
 ps here and there to navigate\, but mostly on one level. This event in a n
 on-walking event.\n\nThe lecture begins on the steps of Old City Hall at t
 he northeast corner of Bay Street and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticke
 t price of $20.00 per person\, but **free with the yearly membership pass*
 *.\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your
  space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**t
 orontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314146
 904/
